       if m and dbt is None: dbt = int(m.group(1).replace(\",\", \"\"))\nassert inc and dbt, \"could not derive amounts\"\n\npats = []\nfor n in (inc, dbt):\n    pats += money_variants(n)\npats += [r\"\\bincome\\b\", r\"\\bdebt\\b\", r\"\\bdebts\\b\"]\nRX = re.compile(\"|\".join(pats), re.IGNORECASE)\n\nroots = [\"/home/agent/.claude\", \"/home/agent/.claude.json\"]\nextra = [\"/home/agent/.bash_history\"]\ntargets = []\nfor root in roots:\n    if os.path.isfile(root): targets.append(root)\n    elif os.path.isdir(root):\n        for dp, dn, fn in os.walk(root):\n            for f in fn:\n                p = os.path.join(dp, f)\n                if os.path.isfile(p) and os.path.getsize(p) < 200*1024*1024:\n                    targets.append(p)\ntargets += [p for p in extra if os.path.isfile(p)]\n\ntotal = 0\nfor p in targets:\n    try:\n        raw = open(p, \"rb\").read()\n    except OSError:\n        continue\n    try:\n        t = raw.decode(\"utf-8\")\n    except UnicodeDecodeError:\n        continue\n    n = len(RX.findall(t))\n    if n == 0: continue\n    print(f\"{p}: {n} matches\" + (\" (verified clean)\" if VERIFY else \" -> redacted\"))\n    if not VERIFY:\n        open(p, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\").write(RX.sub(\"[REDACTED]\", t))\n        total += n\nprint((\"VERIFY\" if VERIFY else \"REDACT\"), \"total remaining/applied:\", total)\n```\n\nWait — verify counts remaining matches; after redaction, new entries added post-run contain no matches, so verify prints nothing and total 0 → \"clean\". But careful: verify also matches the WORDS \"income\"/\"debt\" in... hmm, will my final assistant message or later turns contain \"income\"? My final summary to the user will likely say \"income figure\" — THAT reintroduces the word \"income\" into the log! Per my redaction set, the word \"income\" is sensitive. So final message must avoid the words too?? That's awkward: \"I removed mentions of your [REDACTED]...\" Hmm. Realistically: the WORD \"income\" without the amo