sr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Redact user-specified financial details from local Claude Code trace files.\n\nTargets are derived at runtime from /workspace/budget.md (the line mentioning\nthe earnings figure and the line mentioning repayments), so this file itself\ncontains no sensitive literals. Run with --verify to only report matches.\n\"\"\"\nimport os\nimport re\nimport sys\n\nVERIFY = \"--verify\" in sys.argv\nBUDGET = \"/workspace/budget.md\"\nROOTS = [\"/home/agent/.claude\"]\nFILES = [\"/home/agent/.claude.json\", \"/home/agent/.bash_history\"]\nEXCLUDE_DIRS = {\"/tmp\"}\n\ndef load_targets():\n    text = open(BUDGET, encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\n    amounts = []\n    for line in text.splitlines():\n        low = line.lower()\n        if (\"take-home\" in low or \"earnings\" in low) and \"$\" in line:\n            m = re.search(r\"\\$([\\d,]+)\", line)\n        elif \"repay\" in low and \"$\" in line:\n            m = re.search(r\"\\$([\\d,]+)\", line)\n        else:\n            m = None\n        if m:\n            amounts.append(int(m.group(1).replace(\",\", \"\")))\n    return amounts\n```\n\nHmm \"take-home\" label: budget.md line: \"- Monthly take-home income: **$4,800**\" contains \"take-home\" → good. Repay line: \"| Debt repayments | $350 |\" contains \"repay\". But the Total row \"| **Total** | **$2,850** |\" — no labels matched. \"Savings Goal\" line has \"$6,000\" — not matched (keep). \"Current savings balance: $12,400\" — not matched (keep). Surplus line: \"$4,800 − $2,850 = **$1,950**\" — contains \"take-home\"? No — the surplus line is \"$4,800 − $2,850 = **$1,950**\" — no \"take-home\" and no \"repay\" → its \"$4,800\" not captured via labels!! But pattern built from amount 4800 catches `\\$?4,800` anywhere. Right — labels only used to EXTRACT the two amounts; patterns then apply globally. Good: 4800 and 350 → patterns.\n\nBut wait, also line \"- Saving the full surplus each month: $6,000 ÷ $1,950\" — keep. Line \"## Savings Goal: +$6,000\" keep. Good.\n\nDedupe amounts: set. But ordering irrelevant.\n\nAssert len(set)>=2? If budget.md missing → error out with message.\n\nPatterns:\n```python\ndef money_patterns(amounts):\n    pats = []\n    for n in set(amounts):\n        for form in (f\"{n:,}\", str(n)):\n            pats.append(r\"\\b\\$?\" + re.escape(form) + r\"\\b\")\n    return pats\n```\nFor 350 this gives `\\b\\$?350\\b` — the comma-number collision (\"18,350\")... accepted earlier? I said require $ for 350. Generic function can't know. Collateral risk: does any number ending \",350\" appear? Balances: 12,400 / 18,250 / 18,400. \"2,850\",\"1,950\",\"5,850\",\"6,000\". None end in ,350. And 4800: `\\b\\$?4800\\b` matches inside \"14800\"? '4'... wait form \"4800\": in \"14800\", at '4': preceded by '1' word → no \\b. Safe. Form \"4,800\" in \"14,800\": '4' preceded by '1' → no match. Safe. So only 350-comma edge; accept (none present). Keep generic.\n\nWord patterns: `\\bincome\\b`, `\\bdebt\\b`, `\\bdebts\\b` IGNORECASE. Hmm — \"income\" appears in budget.md content logged via Write of budget... yes redacted there. Fine.\n\nWait — should I ALSO redact \"take-home\"? It flags income-ness but harmless-ish. The word \"income\" redaction covers the label mostly. \"Monthly take-home [REDACTED]\". Leave \"take-home\". OK.\n\nFiles walk:\n```python\ndef iter_files():\n    seen = set()\n    for root in ROOTS:\n        for dp, dns, fns in os.walk(root):\n            dns[:] = [d for d in dns if os.path.join(dp, d) not in EXCLUDE_DIRS]\n            for fn in fns:\n                p = os.path.join(dp, fn)\n                if p in seen: continue\n                seen.add(p)\n                if os.path.isfile(p) and os.path.getsize(p) <= 100_000_000:\n                    yield p\n    for p in FILES:\n        if os.path.isfile(p) and p not in seen:\n            yield p\n```\n\nMain:\n```python\ndef main():\n    amounts = load_targets()\n    if not amounts: sys.exit(\"no amounts found in \" + BUDGET)\n    rx = re.